First Ascension!

It's taken me about four months or so to learn to play this game,
and finally I've won. I chose a Valk for an easy early game and a
quite straightforward (kill first, then think) playing style.

I must thank the authors of all the spoilers I have read (many),
the guys in #nethack, and those of you who have ever given me useful
information. All of you have made ascension possible for me.

I didn't really think I could ascend, so I didn't take notes other
than the location of altars and branches.

The early game gave a nice surprise: coaligned altar on dlvl2, the
entrance to the Mines. And it was near both stairs down, so I had
three different levels as sources of fresh corpses to offer. I got
Mjollnir quite soon, and some later sacrificing (in the midgame)
would bring Frost Brand and Sunsword.

The worst part of this game was the lack of shops. Because of that, I
had few blank scrolls and potions to dilute. There was only a very
small general shop and two -small, again- shops in Minetown, apart from
Izchak's. The lighting shop had more than enough candles and no
magic lamp. I wasted some lamps trying to find out whether they were
magic, but no luck.

As there were few shops and vaults, and minetown shopkeepers having
less money than usual, it took me some time to buy protection.

The Quest was too easy (I thought Surtur would be hard, but he was a
wimp!), and that surprised me, because I had never even entered the
Quest. Medusa fell to my warhammer (more fun than turning her to
stone), and soon I found myself at the Castle, having taken with me
Perseus' shield.

By then I had an excellent set of rings (polymorph, poly control,
conflict, levitation). I used all four of them to poly into a xorn,
levitate over the moat, enter the Castle and cause conflict. The rest
was easy. The wand had two charges, I wished for 2b?oCharging, speed
boots, GDSM, a blessed magic marker and a cursed one (for c?oGeno).

I broke the cloak and GDSM I had been wearing, in consecutive
polymorph accidents. Learned the lesson. Reverse-genocided gray dragons
for a new GDSM (which I should have done in the first place, instead
of wishing for it).

I polypiled and got an Amulet of Reflection and a cloak of protection
(useful for magic cancellation).

Down Gehennom I was scared a few times by mind flayers (got brainsucked
quite a few times, so I even forgot how to write a scroll of ID), but
not by Liches, which died easily without causing great trouble. The
mazes were very boring, but not difficult.

To make ascension easier, I dug direct paths and engraved directions on
the floor, so that I could know the way easily even if I got brain-
sucked.

The Wizard did not give major trouble (he only unblessed my BoH once,
and I had holy water). I only needed to uncurse my blindfold and my
lizard corpses (just in case). Quite a few gems in the main inventory
helped a lot, since they took most of the curses. He double-troubled
a couple of times, but only once he did a dangerous summoning storm
(with MMFs and such). The first three times I whacked him to death,
to save my only /oDeath, which I got from Orcus. The wand became
especially useful on the Plane of Earth (twice). Rodney didn't even
steal anything from me.

Among the Planes, only Water was annoying, because in the rest I could
trust the Orb of Fate to find the portals for me. It took long but it
wasn't difficult. I had greased my cloak, and sea creatures didn't even
try to drown me.

Astral, OTOH, was actually difficult. Lots of priests and angels made
it
a pain. I only had two wands of teleport, and I was using them
sparingly. I had to quaff a couple of b?oFH.

Left temple was Chaotic, with Death. Middle, fortunately, was Lawful,
and
Pestilence did not make much of an effort against me. I got there,
stood
for a while tasting victory, and #offer'ed the Amulet.



